{"id":101,"explanation":"The comment applies to get_user. Caching its result for the lifetime of a process could leave a user's revoked roles in use instead of fetching current data from the database. #640 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"The comment applies to the query and cleanup sequence. Check the error from db.Query before registering rows.Close(), because rows is nil when the query fails.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"The comment explains the setTimeout call around measure(el). The zero-delay timer is a deliberate choice to let layout settle before measuring the element; queueMicrotask would run too soon.","unsure":""}
{"id":104,"explanation":"The comment applies to the token declared as Secret<String>. Its contents must never be logged. Debug output for that type is expected to show a redacted value only; Secret<String> is the referenced type.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"The comment applies to the RetryCount constant. It must be changed together with the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json, which is the referenced configuration file and key.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"The comment applies to the offset passed to ch.map. The offset must be a multiple of pageSize; otherwise the memory mapping rejects it as unaligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"The comment applies to build/ in the rsync command. Its trailing slash tells rsync to copy the contents of that source directory into DEST, rather than copy the directory itself. src means the source argument.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The comment explains the BRIN index on created_at. It states that this index is about 1% the size of a B-tree index and that the events table is appended in time order, making BRIN suitable here.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"The comment applies to the loop that repeatedly checks flag. It calls for replacing this spin wait with a futex; completion means the lock_acquire function in src/sync/lock.c sleeps while waiting. That path and symbol identify the code to check.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"The comment applies to dbo.RebuildStats. The failover section of the runbook, referenced by doc:runbook#failover, explains why this procedure runs on the secondary.","unsure":""}
{"id":111,"explanation":"The comment applies to timeout = 30. The upstream proxy ends idle requests after 60 seconds, so this timeout must stay below 60 seconds.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"The comment applies to Widget's destructor. Making it non-virtual could prevent derived-class destructors from running when a derived object is destroyed through a Widget pointer. #915 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"The comment applies to the foreign_keys PRAGMA. Enable it before any writes on this connection, because the setting applies separately to each connection.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"The comment applies to Name: string[40]. The fixed-length ShortString representation is intentional because the record is written to disk byte for byte; changing it to an ordinary string would change that stored representation.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"The comment applies to the dynamic DELETE statement. Because p_id comes from caller input, pass it as a bound variable, as USING p_id does. Concatenating it into the EXECUTE IMMEDIATE SQL string would allow SQL injection.","unsure":""}
